{"divisionId":3068,"date":"2023-11-27T00:00:00","number":2,"notes":null,"title":"Immigration (Age Assessments) Regulations 2023","isWhipped":true,"isGovernmentContent":false,"authoritativeContentCount":164,"authoritativeNotContentCount":75,"divisionHadTellers":true,"tellerContentCount":164,"tellerNotContentCount":75,"memberContentCount":162,"memberNotContentCount":73,"sponsoringMemberId":4241,"isHouse":true,"isInquorate":false,"amendmentMotionNotes":"<p>Baroness Brinton moved, as an amendment to the motion that the Immigration (Age Assessments) Regulations 2023 be agreed to, at end to insert “but that this House regrets that (1) the Regulations are premature as the policy is still under development, (2) it is unclear whether a person can freely consent to the specified tests, (3) there is no defined mechanism for the Secretary of State to monitor and review the policy, and (4) neither an impact assessment, nor costs associated with the Regulations, have been presented to Parliament for scrutiny; and calls on His Majesty’s Government to withdraw the Regulations until the policy has been developed in full and an impact assessment and costings have been provided to Parliament.” The House divided:</p>","isGovernmentWin":false,"remoteVotingStart":"2023-11-27T19:40:08","remoteVotingEnd":"2023-11-27T19:48:08","divisionWasExclusivelyRemote":false,"contentTellers":[{"memberId":4215,"name":"Lord Stoneham of Droxford","listAs":"Stoneham of Droxford, L.","memberFrom":"Life peer","party":"Liberal Democrat","partyColour":"fc7d0b","partyAbbreviation":"LD","partyIsMainParty":true},{"memberId":4558,"name":"Baroness Thornhill","listAs":"Thornhill, B.","memberFrom":"Life peer","party":"Liberal Democrat","partyColour":"fc7d0b","partyAbbreviation":"LD","partyIsMainParty":true}],"notContentTellers":[{"memberId":4311,"name":"Baroness Williams of Trafford","listAs":"Williams of Trafford, B.","memberFrom":"Life peer","party":"Conservative","partyColour":"0063ba","partyAbbreviation":"Con","p